By the Law of Cosines on triangle $ABC,$
\[\cos \angle ACB = \frac{AC^2 + BC^2 - AB^2}{2 \cdot AC \cdot BC}.\][asy]
unitsize(1 cm);

pair A, B, C, D;

A = (0,2);
B = 2*dir(240);
C = (3,0);
D = (0,0);

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(A--D,dashed);
draw(B--D,dashed);
